mm/page_reporting: report at once what waits to be reported

A guest saved as a template is restored as many times over, each copy
continuing from the moment it was saved. Registering a page reporting
device schedules a first pass over every zone two seconds on, and a guest
saved within those two seconds is saved with the pass still to run: each
copy then reports, two seconds into its life, what its template's boot
freed. Its runs paid for that state: in shards, 50 to 79 us of a 1 ms
command at the median against a guest without the device, 29 us where
the template was saved after the pass.

Add page_reporting.flush, written to report at once what waits to be
reported and to wait for it, pass after pass, until nothing does, as a
guest's agent writes it before the guest is saved. Reporting is as it was
otherwise.

--- a/mm/page_reporting.c
+++ b/mm/page_reporting.c
@@ -417,3 +417,34 @@
 	mutex_unlock(&page_reporting_mutex);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(page_reporting_unregister);
+
+/*
+ * Reports at once what waits to be reported, and waits for it, pass after pass,
+ * until nothing does: what a guest about to be saved has freed is reported before
+ * it is saved, so that no copy of it starts by reporting it.
+ */
+static int page_reporting_flush_set(const char *val, const struct kernel_param *kp)
+{
+	struct page_reporting_dev_info *prdev;
+	int passes;
+
+	mutex_lock(&page_reporting_mutex);
+	prdev = rcu_dereference_protected(pr_dev_info,
+				lockdep_is_held(&page_reporting_mutex));
+	for (passes = 0; prdev && passes < 64; passes++) {
+		if (atomic_read(&prdev->state) == PAGE_REPORTING_IDLE)
+			break;
+		mod_delayed_work(system_freezable_wq, &prdev->work, 0);
+		flush_delayed_work(&prdev->work);
+	}
+	mutex_unlock(&page_reporting_mutex);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static const struct kernel_param_ops page_reporting_flush_ops = {
+	.set = &page_reporting_flush_set,
+};
+
+module_param_cb(flush, &page_reporting_flush_ops, NULL, 0200);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(flush, "Report at once what waits to be reported");
